    "probe_text": "I've read the full flow. Here is every validation and side-effect for `POST /api/owners`, in the order it actually happens. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:135`); V2 only has the paged list.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (`:133`). Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is rejected.\n2. **Bean Validation** on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (declared in the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner`, `OwnersApi.java:85-86`). Applied by Spring before the controller body, per `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`, `@Size 1\u201330`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`, `@Size 1\u201330`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*` (not all-whitespace), `@Size 1\u2013255`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*`, `@Size 1\u201380`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size 1\u201320`\n   - `email` \u2014 optional; when present `@Size 1\u2013255` and `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 optional; when present `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 optional; `@Valid` (no field constraints)\n   - `sharesHousehold` \u2014 optional; no constraint\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Inside `addOwner` (top to bottom)\n\n3. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`, ignoring `id` and `pets` (`:137`, mapper `:101-103`). *(side-effect)*\n4. **Default registration date** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is null, set it to `LocalDate.now()` (`:138-140`). *(side-effect)*\n5. **Roll to next business day** \u2014 `toBusinessDay` pushes Saturday\u2192Monday, Sunday\u2192Monday; weekdays unchanged (`:141`, `:312`). *(side-effect)*\n6. **Daily-cap check** \u2014 count all existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals this owner's (post-roll) date; if `>= 100` return **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS** (`:142-149`). *(validation)*\n7. **Address normalization** \u2014 `addressNormalizer.normalize` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE). If result `isBlank()` return **400** (`:150-153`); otherwise set the normalized address on the owner (`:154`). *(validation + side-effect)*\n8. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 `telephoneNormalizer.normalize` to E.164. If it returns null return **400** (`:155-158`). *(validation)*\n9. **Telephone national-length check** \u2014 `hasValidNationalNumberLength`; if false return **400** (`:159-161`); otherwise set the normalized telephone (`:162`). *(validation + side-effect)*\n10. **Email validation/normalization** \u2014 if email present, trim it; if it fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` return **400** (`:163-168`); otherwise set the trimmed, lower-cased email (`:169`). *(validation + side-effect)*\n11. **Postcode validation** \u2014 if postcode present, it must match `POSTCODE_PATTERN` (4 digits) **and** `cityRegionResolver.isPostcodeValidForCity(city, postcode)`; else return **400** (`:174-180`). *(validation)*\n12. **Household id assignment** \u2014 compute normalized `lastNameKey`/`addressKey`; if `sharesHousehold == true` **and** a matching household already exists, set `householdId` to the shared id (`:187-192`). *(side-effect)*\n13. **Duplicate check** \u2014 if any existing owner has the same derived `identityKey` (normalized telephone `|` email `|` householdId), return **409 CONFLICT** (`:193-195`, `:238-243`). *(validation)*\n14. **City-cap check** \u2014 count existing owners in the same normalized city; if `>= 50` return **409 CONFLICT** (`:196-202`). *(validation)*\n15. **Assign customer code** \u2014 `nextCustomerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is per-city count + 1 (`:203`, `:298`). *(side-effect)*\n16. **Assign namesake count** \u2014 number of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive) (`:204-208`). *(side-effect)*\n17. **Assign membership number** \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>` from the registration year (`:209`, `:325`). *(side-effect)*\n18. **Set bulk-signup warning** \u2014 `true` when `ownersCreatedThatDay > 80` (the count from step 6) (`:210`). *(side-effect)*\n19. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`:211`). *(side-effect)*\n20. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel (`:212-214`). *(side-effect)*\n21. **Build response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto` (which computes displayName, initials, membershipLevel, locality, contactPreference, identityKey), set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED** (`:215-218`). *(side-effect)*\n\nA couple of notes worth flagging while reading, not fixing:\n- The `>= 100` daily cap (step 6) and the `bulkSignupWarning > 80` flag (step 18) both use `ownersCreatedThatDay`, computed once against the post-business-day-roll date.\n- Step 7 sets the normalized address, then step 12 re-normalizes `owner.getAddress()` for the household key \u2014 harmless because `normalize` is idempotent.\n- `clinicService.findAllOwners()` is re-queried separately at steps 6, 13, 14, 15, and 16."
